<p><b>Workspace → Preferences… → Desktop</b> sets how the whole desktop looks and behaves. Changes apply at once, in every app.</p>
<p><b>Choose your style</b> picks a set of settings in one click:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Style</th><th>Gives you</th></tr>
  <tr><td><b>NeXT</b></td><td>Floating menus at the top left and the Dock down the right, as on NeXTSTEP.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Mac</b></td><td>A menu bar across the top and a see-through Dock along the bottom.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><b>Windows</b></td><td>Menus inside each window and a taskbar along the bottom.</td></tr>
</table>
<p>You can then change any one setting on its own:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Dock position</b>: right, left, top or bottom. With the Mac menu bar the Dock can't be at the top.</li>
  <li><b>Menu style</b>: NeXT's floating menus, a Mac menu bar, or menus in each window.</li>
  <li><b>Minimize windows</b>: into NeXT miniwindows, into the Dock, or as previews.</li>
  <li><b>Dock style</b>, <b>Scroller style</b> and <b>Window style</b>: the NeXT, Mac or Windows look of each. The window style also decides what <kbd>Return</kbd> does to a selected file: the Mac style renames it, NeXT and Windows open it.</li>
  <li><b>Appearance</b>: Dark or Light.</li>
  <li><b>Desktop icons</b>: what's in your Desktop folder is always on the desktop. <b>Files, folders and disks</b> adds the startup disk, NextBSD, and each disk you connect. The Mac style shows the disks; NeXT and Windows show <b>Files and folders</b> only. Icons line up from the top corner, disks first, and move up when one goes away. An icon you drag stays where you put it, until <b>Clean Up</b> or <b>Sort By</b> lines them all up again.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each setting starts at <b>Use theme default</b> (Desktop icons at <b>Use style default</b>). Choosing that again goes back to the theme's or the style's choice.</p>
